<title>USA: Borg-Warner sees layoffs from GM strike.</title>
<headline>Borg-Warner sees layoffs from GM strike.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Borg-Warner Automotive Inc said Friday it expected to lay off up to 70 temporary employees at its Frankfort, Ill. plant because of the two-week-old strike against the Canadian operations of General Motors Corp.</p>
<p>Borg-Warner Automotive supplies GM with parts. The business accounts for about 25 percent of Borg's revenues.</p>
<p>The plant, which employs about 480 workers, makes transmission components.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
